# W11-9b: Desktop identity — fonts + GTK theme deps (DEC-PHASE11-013, DEC-PHASE11-010)
#
# @decision DEC-PHASE11-013
# @title W11-9b: Font pair Iosevka (OFL-1.1) + Hack (Apache-2.0)
# @status accepted
# @rationale Operator directive 2026-07-13: community-developed fonts only;
#   no vendor-proprietary or vendor-adjacent monospace fonts permitted per
#   DEC-PHASE11-013. Iosevka is an OFL-1.1 monospace coding font well-suited
#   to the terminal aesthetic. Hack is an Apache-2.0 secondary fallback
#   (formerly Bitstream Vera). Both are community-developed with no vendor
#   telemetry surface (rejected alternatives: vendor-adjacent fonts — see
#   MASTER_PLAN.md DEC-PHASE11-013 row for the full rejected-list rationale).
#   fonts-iosevka is available in Debian Bullseye (package fonts-iosevka).
#   fonts-hack-otf provides the OpenType flavour; check:
#     apt-cache policy fonts-iosevka fonts-hack-otf
#   Both confirmed available in Bullseye main. No tarball fallback needed.
#   papirus-icon-theme: base for Orion-X-Icons inheritance (Orion-X-Icons/
#   index.theme sets Inherits=Papirus-Dark; Papirus is ~9 MB compressed in Bullseye).
#   gtk2-engines-murrine: required for GTK2 Adwaita-dark derivation (Orion-X-Cyberdeck
#   gtk-2.0/gtkrc). Absent → GTK2 apps in the session fall back to Raleigh theme.
#
# fonts-iosevka: Iosevka monospace (OFL-1.1) — primary terminal + monospace font
# TEMPORARILY COMMENTED — fonts-iosevka is NOT in bullseye (first packaged in bookworm).
# The historical comment at line 230 claiming "available in Debian Bullseye" was wrong;
# `apt-cache policy fonts-iosevka` returns Candidate: (none) in bullseye main/contrib/
# non-free/backports. Reinstate via one of: (a) sideload bookworm .deb into
# iso/config/packages.chroot/, (b) upstream Iosevka .deb from GitHub release, or
# (c) move base image to bookworm (larger project change). Tracked as GH issue #85.
#fonts-iosevka
# fonts-hack-otf: Hack OTF (Apache-2.0) — secondary monospace font
fonts-hack-otf
# gtk2-engines-murrine: Murrine GTK2 engine (required for Adwaita-dark GTK2 variants)
gtk2-engines-murrine
# papirus-icon-theme: Papirus icon theme (GPL-3.0+) — base for Orion-X-Icons inheritance
papirus-icon-theme
# W11-9b Themes & Runtime: xfconf provides xfconf-query (P0-001, QA_AUDIT_2026-07-21)
# xfconf-query is called by toggle-theme.sh:60-67 at runtime to apply XFCE wallpaper and
# theme changes. Absent → runtime theme toggle silently degrades (P0 bricking bug).
# @decision DEC-PHASE11-016
# @title QA P0-001: xfconf added to package list (provides xfconf-query for toggle-theme.sh)
# @status accepted
# @rationale tmp/QA_AUDIT_2026-07-21.md P0-001: toggle-theme.sh calls xfconf-query -c
#   xfce4-desktop but xfconf was not in the package list. XFCE4 runtime (not just static
#   XML seeding) requires xfconf to apply wallpaper/theme changes. Silent fallback at
#   toggle-theme.sh:67 masked the failure in unit tests. Fix: add xfconf explicitly.
xfconf

