suricata

# Custom packages (will be installed from config/packages.chroot/)
# orionx-custom-tools
# orionx-theme

# DEC-PHASE12-043: MaxMind-format database reader for the attack map's
# optional geolocation labels. The READER ships; the DATABASE does not.
#
# Splitting them this way is deliberate. GeoLite2 cannot be redistributed in
# an image at all, and DB-IP Lite (CC BY 4.0) can but is republished monthly,
# so a baked-in copy would rot silently inside an ISO built once and run for
# months (/opt/orionx/osint/GEOIP.txt). The database therefore arrives via
# /opt/orionx/optional/install-geoip.sh — or on a USB stick from another
# machine, which only works if the reader is already here. ~150 KB.
#
# With neither reader nor database the map still works and still shows every
# source; public sources are labelled UNLOCATED and never given a position.
python3-maxminddb
